# seo-agent configuration
#
# EVERY VARIABLE HERE IS OPTIONAL, and the free path is the intended one.
#
# 28 of the 36 tools run at no cost. With nothing configured at all you can
# already crawl and audit any site, mine keywords from autocomplete, cluster
# them into a content plan, score drafts, analyse internal link equity, plan a
# programmatic SEO set and validate it before publishing.
#
# Run `node dist/cli.js capabilities` to see what's currently active.
# Legend: ✓ full   ~ available but partial   ✗ off

# ===========================================================================
# STAYING FREE
# ===========================================================================
# Set this and no metered call can ever be made — the refusal happens before
# the network request, so a stray API key in your environment cannot spend
# anything. Free tools are unaffected and keep working normally.
#
# SEO_AGENT_BUDGET=0
#
# If you later decide to use a paid provider, replace the 0 with a real unit
# ceiling (e.g. 500) rather than removing the line.

# ===========================================================================
# FREE CREDENTIALS — the recommended setup, in priority order
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Search Console — free forever, and the highest-value thing to configure
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unlocks: seo_gsc_sites, seo_gsc_performance, seo_gsc_opportunities
#
# Search Console reports the impressions, clicks, CTR and position Google
# actually recorded for your site. Ahrefs and Semrush *estimate* these from a
# sampled keyword universe; this is ground truth, and it covers every query you
# surface for rather than only the ones you thought to track. It is also what
# makes seo_gsc_opportunities work — striking-distance queries, CTR gaps,
# cannibalisation, content decay and rising queries, all found mechanically.
#
# Setup:
#   1. console.cloud.google.com, signed in with a PERSONAL Google account.
#      New project -> leave Location as "No organization". See the note below.
#   2. APIs & Services -> enable "Google Search Console API".
#   3. IAM -> Service Accounts -> Create. No project roles are needed; it never
#      touches Cloud resources, only Search Console.
#   4. Keys -> Add key -> JSON -> download.
#   5. Search Console -> your property -> Settings -> Users and permissions ->
#      add the service account's ...@....iam.gserviceaccount.com address.
#      "Restricted" is enough; this tool only reads.
#   6. Verify with: node dist/cli.js seo_gsc_sites
#
# Why "No organization" matters: since 2024-05-03 Google enforces the security
# baseline org policy `iam.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation` on newly created
# organizations, which blocks the JSON key download at step 4 no matter what
# roles you hold. Projects with no organization are not subject to it. If you
# are on a Workspace account and cannot avoid an org, use the OAuth block below
# instead — the constraint does not apply to OAuth clients.
#
# GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON accepts either the JSON contents or a path to the file.
# GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=/path/to/service-account.json
# GSC_SITE_URL=sc-domain:example.com
#
# The property string must match Search Console exactly. Domain properties look
# like "sc-domain:example.com"; URL-prefix properties look like
# "https://example.com/" (note the trailing slash). Run seo_gsc_sites to list
# what the credential can actually see before wiring it into an agent.
#
# OAuth alternative — use this if an org policy blocks service account keys:
# GSC_CLIENT_ID=
# GSC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GSC_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# GSC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Core Web Vitals — free key
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unlocks: seo_page_speed
#
# console.cloud.google.com -> enable "PageSpeed Insights API" -> APIs & Services
# -> Credentials -> Create API key. A plain API key, not a service account, so
# no org policy can block it.
#
# The unkeyed endpoint is rate-limited to uselessness, which is why a key is
# required rather than optional.
# PAGESPEED_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Domain authority — free tier
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unlocks: seo_domain_authority, and personalises seo_keyword_difficulty so
# difficulty is scored relative to your domain rather than in the abstract.
#
# Register at https://openpagerank.com — no card, no trial.
#
# Open PageRank returns authority scores ONLY. seo_backlinks and seo_link_gap
# need real link-level data and stay unavailable; capabilities reports this
# capability as "~ partial" rather than pretending otherwise.
# OPENPAGERANK_API_KEY=

# ===========================================================================
# PAID PROVIDERS — entirely optional, all off by default
# ===========================================================================
# Leave this whole section commented out to stay free. Everything below is
# additive: nothing already working degrades if you never configure any of it.
#
# If you do add one, set SEO_AGENT_BUDGET to a real ceiling first. Agents loop,
# and a research chain with no cap will fire thousands of metered calls.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live SERP data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unlocks: seo_serp, seo_rank_check, seo_competitors_discover, seo_content_gap,
# and competitively-grounded seo_content_brief.
#
# There is no free option here. I verified this rather than assuming it: Bing's
# HTML endpoint serves a CAPTCHA to server traffic and DuckDuckGo's lite
# endpoint returns an empty document, so scraping is not a viable path.
#
# Without it: Search Console covers your own rankings (better data, free), and
# seo_page_inspect analyses any competitor URL directly.
#
# Pick ONE. First one found wins, in this order:
#
# Serper — cheapest and fastest, generous free tier. https://serper.dev
# SERPER_API_KEY=
#
# SerpApi — richest SERP feature parsing. https://serpapi.com
# SERPAPI_KEY=
#
# DataForSEO — the only one that ALSO provides keyword volume and backlinks, so
# one credential unlocks three capabilities. https://dataforseo.com
# DATAFORSEO_LOGIN=
# DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Search volume, CPC, and full backlink data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unlocks: seo_keyword_metrics, seo_backlinks, seo_link_gap.
# Uses the DataForSEO credentials above.
#
# Without it, volume is returned as null with an explanation rather than being
# guessed, and difficulty falls back to a lexical estimate that always carries
# method: "lexical" and confidence: 0.35. A fabricated search volume is the
# single most damaging thing this tool could return — an agent will build a
# whole content calendar on it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI search visibility
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unlocks: seo_ai_visibility, which asks an assistant the questions a buyer
# would ask (with live web search) and measures whether your brand gets
# recommended, how it is described, and who takes share of voice.
#
# Metered per query — this is the most expensive tool here, so it reserves
# against SEO_AGENT_BUDGET before spending rather than after.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ===========================================================================
# Crawler behaviour
# ===========================================================================
# SEO_AGENT_MAX_PAGES=500          # default page budget per crawl
# SEO_AGENT_CONCURRENCY=5          # parallel requests
# SEO_AGENT_HOST_DELAY_MS=250      # minimum gap between requests to one host
# SEO_AGENT_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# SEO_AGENT_USER_AGENT="Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; seo-agent/0.1) AgentSEOBot"

# Set to 1 to ignore robots.txt. Only for sites you own — an agent crawling on
# someone's behalf can get an IP or an office blocked, and "the model decided to
# ignore robots.txt" is not a defensible answer.
# SEO_AGENT_IGNORE_ROBOTS=0

# ===========================================================================
# Defaults and limits
# ===========================================================================
# SEO_AGENT_LOCATION="United States"
# SEO_AGENT_DEVICE=desktop

# Language for keyword expansion, intent detection, readability scoring and
# generated page copy. Supported: en, es, es-AR. Setting it here saves passing
# `language` on every call.
# SEO_AGENT_LANGUAGE=en

# Where crawls, keywords, rank history and the response cache live.
# SEO_AGENT_DATA_DIR=~/.seo-agent

# Rows returned inline before a result spills to an artifact file. Keeps large
# result sets from flooding an agent's context window.
# SEO_AGENT_MAX_INLINE_ROWS=100
